      "crates/terra-sandbox/src/transport/model.rs"
    ],
    "ground": "Decode grayscale PNG samples as min_height + pixel/65535 * height_span, round each to f32, bilinearly sample the source at level-15 geographic tile knots for a 65x65 height field, then bilinearly sample the four enclosing tile knots and round to f32. This reproduces the native resident terrain-height path. The authored source features contain no bridge, water or building replacement at these positions.",
    "support": "Transform the avatar centre, four 0.275 m half-width corners and four edge midpoints through the WGS84 local frame, then sample the reconstructed resident height. Approximate native slope from five-metre east/west and north/south height differences.",
    "clearance": "Transform saved positions through the WGS84 ECEF/local-frame equations. Test projected oriented-rectangle intervals on both bodies horizontal axes plus the explicit ground-base vertical interval, using actual registered model dimensions and the living reference dimensions for other actor kinds. Human contact footprints use the current axis-aligned reference mapping. The avatar is excluded from its own occupancy query.",
    "distance": "Surface separation uses terra-core mean-radius great-circle distance; local tangent centre distance is also reported because it is a different metric.",
    "invariants": "Compare parsed JSON records directly across after-exit, first-exit, resumed-checkpoint and final; permit ordinary clock and needs progression."
  },
